      "text": "1. We start with the given expression: \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\).\n2. To combine these fractions, we find a common denominator. The common denominator for the two fractions is \\((3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)\\).\n3. Compute the denominator:\n   \\[\n   (3 - 5i)(3 + 5i) = 3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 - 25i^2 = 9 - 25(-1) = 9 + 25 = 34.\n   \\]\n4. Thus, the expression becomes:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i)}{34} + \\frac{(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i)}{34}.\n   \\]\n5. Simplify the numerators by expanding both binomials:\n   \\[\n   (3 + 5i)(3 + 5i) = 9 + 15i + 15i + 25i^2 = 9 + 30i + 25(-1) = 9 + 30i - 25 = -16 + 30i,\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (3 - 5i)(3 - 5i) = 9 - 15i - 15i + 25i^2 = 9 - 30i + 25(-1) = 9 - 30i - 25 = -16 - 30i.\n   \\]\n6. Substitute these back into the expression:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{-16 + 30i}{34} + \\frac{-16 - 30i}{34}.\n   \\]\n7. Combine the fractions:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{(-16 + 30i) + (-16 - 30i)}{34} = \\frac{-16 + 30i - 16 - 30i}{34} = \\frac{-32}{34} = -\\frac{16}{17}.\n   \\]\n8. Thus, the simplified value of the given expression is \\(\\boxed{-\\frac{16}{17}}\\).",
